WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.971
-Did you know that Clementine
was my grandfather's?

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.506
-Yeah.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.808
-He named it
after his mother.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.542
Oh, boy.

00:00:10.542 --> 00:00:14.613
He was a very strict man.

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:17.083
But I always
found him reasonable.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:22.622 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.690
And he had a policy.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.894
He would only kill
if it was absolutely necessary.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.262
[ Gun cocks ]

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.130
For food...

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.634
or to vanquish an enemy...

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:39.072
or to eliminate
an incompetent imbecile.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.775
-Mistakes were made.
It won't happen again.

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:45.210
-Oh, I know it won't.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.812
-Oh!
[ Laughs ]

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.681
-That's a real dramatic --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.817
Real dramatic clip.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.418
-We're back of Bryan Cranston.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.355
That was a clip from "Argylle."
A great cast.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.623
Rob Delaney was in that clip.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.357
-Another great comedian actor.
-Yeah, very funny.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:01.127
-Dua Lipa -- my good friend
Dua Lipa was in the film.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:05.831
-I heard and saw that --
that clip of you.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.700
-Yeah.
-You were imbibing a little bit.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.302
-We imbibed.
-You were imbibing.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.070
-Now you did not have
a scene with Dua,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.307
so you don't know
that she's a bully.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.441
-Is she really?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.010
She bullied me into
getting my first tattoo.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.014
-Through what? What was her --
her way into bullying you?

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.316
-She is Dua Lipa, and she asked.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.084
[ Laughter ]
-That -- That is.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.786
-That's horrible of her.
-That's horrible!

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.321
-Horrible.
-What else was I gonna say?

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.689
-Yes.
-Now, you got a tattoo

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:32.758
with Aaron Paul.
Matching tattoo.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.126
-Yeah. Well, they're not
matching tattoos.

00:01:34.126 --> 00:01:35.328
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:38.431
-The last day of production,
11 years ago,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.567
I got a tattoo on my hand,
but you can't see it.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:42.835
-Okay.
-Because, an actor,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.537
I don't want to have it social.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.840
-But I did get it right there.
-Wow. Very good.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.475
There's --
Yeah, the "BB." There you go.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.877
-It's the symbol
for "Breaking Bad."

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.547
And someone said,
"Why put it there?"

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.516
No one else can see it.
And I said,

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.352
"Well, it's not really
for someone else, it's for me."

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:03.189
And when I catch it, I remember
the times that we had

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.825
on this wonderful show.
-Do you want to see

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.026
my matching tattoo?
-I do.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.427
I want to see your tattoo.
-Okay.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.662
Here we go. Ready?
-Yeah.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.064
You guys got it over there?
Okay. Here we go.

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:14.033
Here we go.
-Ah!

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.135
Very nice!
[ Applause ]

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.403
-There we go.
Her call, not mine.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.838
-Very nice.
Yeah.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.307
-No, actually, here's, uh --
here's the real one right there.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.808
It's that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.077
-No, I thi--
I think that's just a mole.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.379
-Yeah, well, guess what.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:28.814
John Oliver,
who's a very cruel person,

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:31.216
he said
it looks like a tick.

00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:32.952
-Yeah, yeah!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.820
So that's like --
the rest of every summer,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.288
the rest of my life,
my wife's gonna be like,

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:39.492
"Check for ticks," and I'm like,
"It's not a tick."

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.793
-Now, it's kind of
a personal thing.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.196
-Yeah.
-So, a very attractive

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.597
young woman...
-Yeah.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.133
-...convinces you to get
a matching tattoo?

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.068
-Yeah.
-What did your wife

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.503
say about that?
-We -- You know what?

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.004
It's funny. We're trying
not to talk about it.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.539
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.207
-I won't bring it up.

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:56.909
I'm sorry I brought it up.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.645
-I mean, I feel like
we talk about it,

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.681
like, non-verbally,
with a lot of sighs.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.882
-Yeah and looks and side eye.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.884
-A lot of looks
and a lot of sighs.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.553
Now, of course, mine is a --
is a temporary tattoo.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:10.222
But a lot of people
did get Heisenberg tattoos.

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.091
-Oh, God, yeah.
-And you've gotten to learn

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.260
over the years.
I mean, these are intense.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.796
-Yeah, that's on an arm.
-That's on an arm.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.465
-Got the RV and everything.
That's on a neck.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.033
-That's a neck.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.102
-He's, like, pulling down --
-This is a fun one.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.670
Just on the back of a head.
-Yeah.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.872
He carved it out on his head.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.474
-Yeah.
And then this one -- this is --

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.710
Well, I mean,
that's just a human butt.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.445
-That's, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.345
That's on a butt.

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.615
Now, if you look closely
to this,

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:40.620
uh, on the left, you see Larry,
and Moe is down below.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.691
So I'm actually the third Stooge
on someone's ass.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.761
-I just like -- there's some
lady out there who loves

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.230
"Breaking Bad" and the Stooges
and saw this guy's butt,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.599
and is like, "He's a keeper."
-"He's a Stooge."

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.168
-"He's the guy."
-Actually, they must have

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.236
thought I was Curly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.172
"Oh, he's bald.
That's Curly."

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.541
-Uh, you got to work
in the film

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:04.377
not only with great actors,
but there's a cat named Alfie.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.878
-[ Breathes deeply ]
Yeah.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.179
-Oh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:09.582
It did not go well?
-I hate that cat.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.451
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:15.421
That cat thinks he's
"Oh, big show business" now.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.456
He's stealing every scene.
-He --

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.291
-You know what?
He walks down the hall.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:21.995
You're not supposed to look him
directly in the eye.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.963
I mean, it's like
you're supposed to...

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.932
He's got his agents following
him around and everything.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:28.367
-I mean, I will say
that's problematic

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.870
because even unfamous
cats are ass [bleep].

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.071
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.640
So they're all starting
at a place of the worst.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.143
-They're the worst,
and they get even worse.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.978
Yes.
-Was Alfie the name --

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.913
Uh, that's the cat's name.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.215
-Well, the name of the real
cat...

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:44.550
-Okay.
-...is Chip.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.087
-Okay. Gotcha.
-And Chip is, um...

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.123
owned by a supermodel.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.291
-Isn't that the --

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:53.526
-So. there's Claudia Schiffer
right there.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.328
-Yes.
-And that's -- so Chip the cat

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:57.729
actually gets carried
around in this case.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:59.832
-Yes. Carried around.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.901
I would like to be carried
around in a case like that.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.137
And, in fact,
by Claudia Schiffer,

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:07.340
I would like to crawl in --
Okay.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.708
Um, actually,
and that's where, you know,

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:12.244
they talked about,
uh, the Taylor Swift.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:16.648
There was rumor that
Taylor Swift wrote "Argylle."

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:21.354
And while I cannot deny
or confirm that, apparently,

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:25.691
Taylor Swift has a cat in a --
in a cat carrier like that,

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:28.060
and so they thought
there was a tie-in to it.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.528
-Gotcha.
Now, this must have been

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:31.197
the hardest
acting you've ever done.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:34.433
You had to actually act
and hold the same case.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.668
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.668 --> 00:05:38.203
-Yes. Um...
-Yeah.

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:39.739
-And I'm --
I'm allergic to cats.

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:42.208
-Yeah.
-Well, I'm mostly allergic

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.109
to the musical "Cats," but...
-Yeah.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.377
[ Laughter ]
A lot of people --

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:46.779
That's one
of the more common allergies.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.649
-Yeah, but also
the actual feline.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:52.017
-Yeah.
-It makes my eyes water.

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:55.721
Um, yeah, I -- my character
doesn't like cats,

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:59.325
and so he mistreated
the fake cat.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.794
We had a real cat
and fake cat.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:05.998
Chip was not only treated
like a star, that he is --

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:10.135
he was on the phone during
the breaks calling Scorsese.

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:13.138
And, you know, it's like,
"Uh, what's next for me?"

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:14.806
-And on speaker, right?
So you could all hear.

00:06:14.806 --> 00:06:16.909
-On speaker!
So we're like...

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.210
-"We know --
you got connections, Chip."

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.378
-So classless.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.380
-Well, again, it speaks to you
as an actor

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.949
that I've only heard
great things

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:25.451
about how you interacted
with Chip, who you clearly hate.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.253
-I clearly hate him.
Yeah.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.855
But, you know,
he is the star of this movie.

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:32.858
-Yeah.
-Which I am, uh, very sad about.

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.159
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:35.928
-The movie is fun, however.
-The movie is fun.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.196
-Oh, my God, it's so much fun.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.331
-And thanks for being here.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.565
It's always so much fun
to see you.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:42.001
Always such a pleasure.
You guys, Bryan Cranston.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:44.303
"Argylle," theaters and IMAX,
February 2nd.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.239
Stick around. We'll be
right back with Lola Tung.

